+    With the optional ``levels`` argument, you can perform hierarchical
+    grouping. When ``levels`` is a positive integer, the ``attribute``
+    argument can be either a comma-separated string or a sequence of
+    attributes, one for each level. Each result group retains the
+    grouper/list interface; intermediate lists contain child groups
+    and the final lists contain the original items.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for dept, roles in users|groupby("department,role", levels=2) %}
+          <li>{{ dept }}
+            <ul>{% for role, members in roles %}
+              <li>{{ role }}: {{ members|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}
+            {% endfor %}</ul>
+          </li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    Omitting ``levels`` keeps the ordinary single-attribute behavior.
+    A one-element attribute list is also accepted. Multiple attributes
+    without ``levels``, mismatched attribute counts, and nonpositive or
+    noninteger ``levels`` raise :exc:`FilterArgumentError`.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
     .. versionchanged:: 2.6
         The attribute supports dot notation for nested access.
+
+    .. versionadded:: NEXT.VERSION
+        Added the ``levels`` parameter for hierarchical grouping.
